      "card_ids": ["C54","C57"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Cefixime and cefadroxil are PEPT1 substrates, supporting carrier-mediated intestinal uptake as a class feature relevant to the query cephem prodrug.",
      "card_ids": ["C55","C61"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Atenolol, a low-permeability Caco-2 marker with Papp around 4 to 8 x 10^-7 cm/s and 2.12 x 10^-6 cm/s in IEC layers, has human oral bioavailability of about 50% to 63%, showing low in vitro permeability does not imply F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C09","C20","C63"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Amorphous cefuroxime axetil achieved 100% dissolution within 60 minutes and bacampicillin hydrochloride has adequate aqueous solubility, supporting prodrug ester solubility for oral absorption.",
