      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C56","C58","C59","C60","C62","C64","C65"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the exact query molecule.",
    "The query differs from cefuroxime axetil at C7 (1-hydroxyethyl versus furan methoxyimino acetamido) and in ester alkyl (acetoxymethyl versus 1-acetoxyethyl); impact on PEPT1 affinity and esterase stability is unmeasured.",
    "No query-specific PEPT1 transport, efflux, or intestinal metabolism data are available.",
    "Prodrug ester hydrolysis before absorption could reduce systemic exposure of the active cephem, though the prodrug itself is the absorbed species.",
    "Meropenem Caco-2 permeability records are for a non-prodrug carbapenem and do not directly inform the query prodrug."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because the closest transferable human record (cefuroxime axetil F=64%) and all human beta-lactam F records support F >= 20%; L5 adds PEPT1-mediated uptake evidence for cefuroxime axetil and other cephems, strengthening the absorption mechanism for this acyloxyalkyl ester cephem prodrug. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20%."
}

